      "id": "a9759a92-5bdb-5c9f-a134-2c0c8c77df14",
      "document_id": "tech/lfi-api-hub/v2.1/consent-management-interface/bank-service-initiation/requirements",
      "type": "intro",
      "text": "CMI — Bank Service Initiation Requirements\n\nThe tables below define the display, labelling, and behavioural requirements for the Bank Service Initiation\n consents (Single Instant Payment and Multi Payment) in the LFI Consent Management Interface (CMI). See the User Experience\n page for interactive wireframes of the dashboard and detail pages.\n\nThe LFI CMI shares the same structure and consent-type logic as the TPP CMI for Bank Service Initiation\n, with the differences noted below. Adjustments to the requirements below are permitted provided the customer can always clearly understand what consents they have granted. Any adjustments must be documented in your CX certification submission.",
      "metadata": {
        "title": "CMI — Bank Service Initiation Requirements",
        "source_repo": "Nebras-Open-Finance/community-standards",
        "source_file": "src/pages/tech/lfi-api-hub/v2.1/consent-management-interface/bank-service-initiation/requirements.vue",
